From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: aperture: wait briefly for the default camera instead of starting the first one listed

Through the camera portal, the PipeWire remote Snapshot gets lists no camera when the device provider starts:
the portal grants the node permissions a moment later, so the cameras arrive one by one as DeviceAdded (on the
SM-T550 the front ~1 ms before the back). The viewfinder's camera-added handler started the FIRST arrival
without asking the provider for the default camera, so Snapshot sometimes opened the front camera although
last-camera-id named the back one (and did not save that pick, so the setting still said Back).

Now a camera that arrives while the viewfinder is loading (or has no camera) is started at once only if it is
the default camera; otherwise the viewfinder waits DEFAULT_CAMERA_GRACE_MS (300 ms, one timer) and then starts
the default camera or the first one. init() does the same when only part of the cameras is listed. A camera
that appears while the viewfinder is in the Error state is still started at once, as before.
